---
title: "Multi-value register: concurrent writes become siblings"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant L0 as r1
    participant L1 as r2
    Note over L0: write<br/>A:1→"draft"
    L0->>L1: #8203;
    Note over L1: sync<br/>A:1→"draft"
    Note over L0: write<br/>A:2→"edit A"
    Note over L1: write<br/>B:1→"edit B"
    L0->>L1: #8203;
    Note over L1: sync<br/>A:2→"edit A"<br/>B:1→"edit B"
    L1->>L0: #8203;
    Note over L0: sync<br/>A:2→"edit A"<br/>B:1→"edit B"
    Note over L1,L0: r1 and r2 agree: A:2 and B:1 are siblings, since neither writer was shown the other's value
    Note over L1: write<br/>B:2→"merged"
    L1->>L0: #8203;
    Note over L0: sync<br/>B:2→"merged"
    Note over L0: sync (stale)<br/>B:2→"merged"
    Note over L1,L0: a copy of r2 taken right after its first sync still holds A:1, but r1 has already seen that write, so "draft" is not resurrected
